{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalForms"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.normal_forms_preserved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.normal_forms_preserved","kind":"axiom","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L133-L165","doc":"The set of normal-form monomials is unchanged between the\ndeformed algebra and its associated graded.\n\nAxiomatised because the proof requires establishing an indexing\ncorrespondence between the rule lists of the two systems (matching\n`List.mem` witnesses to `List.get` indices), then applying\n`h_same_lm` to transfer the `isInfix` negation.  This bookkeeping\nrequires `List.indexOf`-based lemmas not available in Mathlib's\n`List.isInfix` API.\n\nThe argument is straightforward: `isNormalForm` only depends on the\nleading monomials of the rules (via the `isInfix` check), and the\nhypothesis `h_same_lm` asserts these are identical.  Hence the\nnormal-form predicate is the same for both systems.\n\nReference: Bergman 1978, §5 (filtered deformations preserve\nthe leading-term ideal). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.dist_flat_deformation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.dist_flat_deformation","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L105-L129","doc":"**Flat deformation of distribution algebras** ([fred2005, Theorem 3.15]):\n\nThe distribution algebra `Dist(G)` of the non-commutative formal\ngroup `G / ℤ_p` is a flat deformation of `Dist(H)`, the\ndistribution algebra of the commutative base group `H / 𝔽_p`.\n\nThis means:\n- `Dist(G)` and `Dist(H)` have the same `k`-dimension in each\n  filtration degree.\n- The multiplication on `Dist(G)` reduces to that on `Dist(H)`\n  modulo lower filtration degrees.\n- The GS normal forms for `Dist(G)` coincide with the PBW\n  (divided-power) basis of `Dist(H)`.\n\nThis is the algebraic content of the statement that the\nintegration of a skewed-Poisson structure produces a genuine\ndeformation, not a degeneration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.gs_implies_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.gs_implies_flat","kind":"axiom","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L77-L101","doc":"**GS basis implies flatness**: if the defining relations of a\nfiltered algebra form a GS basis (under a filtration-compatible\nadmissible order), then the algebra is a flat deformation of its\nassociated graded.\n\nConcretely: the normal-form monomials of degree `≤ n` form a basis\nof `Fₙ`, and their images in `gr_n` form a basis of the `n`-th\ngraded piece.  Since the normal-form monomials are the same in\nboth the deformed and undeformed settings, the Hilbert function\nis preserved.\n\nThe proof uses the composition lemma: normal-form monomials are\na basis (by `composition_lemma`).  The same monomials, projected\nto the associated graded, are a basis of `gr` (since they are\nhomogeneous by construction of the deg-lex order).\n\nReference: [fred2005, Theorem 3.15], Bergman 1978 §5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isFlat","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L73-L75","doc":"**Flatness**: two filtered algebras have the same Hilbert function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HilbertFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HilbertFunction","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L64-L69","doc":"The **Hilbert function** `H(n)` of a filtered algebra: the dimension\nof the `n`-th graded piece `Fₙ / F_{n-1}`.\n\nRepresented abstractly as a function `ℕ → ℕ` (or `ℕ → ℕ∞` for\ninfinite-dimensional algebras). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.filtrationDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.filtrationDegree","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The **degree** of a homogeneous element in a filtered algebra:\nthe smallest `n` such that `a ∈ Fₙ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.mul_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.mul_compat","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The filtration is compatible with multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.exhaustive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.exhaustive","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The filtration is exhaustive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.ascending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.ascending","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The filtration is ascending. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.filt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.filt","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The `n`-th filtration piece (as a predicate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration","kind":"structure","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L45-L56","doc":"A **filtration** on an algebra `A`: an ascending chain of\n`k`-submodules `F₀ ⊆ F₁ ⊆ F₂ ⊆ ...` with `⋃ Fₙ = A` and\n`Fₘ · Fₙ ⊆ F_{m+n}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}